.TH git-harvest-init 1  "init " 
.SH NAME
git\-harvest\-init \- Write a fresh CHANGELOG carrying the default configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-harvest init\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write a fresh CHANGELOG carrying the default configuration.
.PP
Writes a starter CHANGELOG carrying the default harvest configuration — the commit\-message grammar, the accepted change buckets and the default renderer — so a repository has something for `scan` and `assemble` to read and write to from its very first commit.  Refuses to overwrite an existing CHANGELOG unless told to.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: CHANGELOG.ron]
The path to write the CHANGELOG to
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite the target when it exists already
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
